  "lifetime": "Synchronous owned children and OF refs; remove split consumers, macros, then clock manager. Keep platform data and parent clocks alive through child teardown. Component cleanup drains WCD calls, Type-C and snd_event before reverse macro exits. Provider removal closes and drains active operations without holding the operation mutex over callbacks. Registration/removal must not be called from a callback being drained.",
  "borrowed_pointer_contract": "Native device getters remain borrowed: callers must serialize against driver removal. A device reference alone does not retain devres. Internal resource-clock calls hold the parent operation gate for their entire call.",
  "typec_gate": "Preserved native presence of qcom,unsupported-typec-analog-acc. Successful init has component-specific exit before card destruction.",
  "clock_ownership": "Track successful owned CCF enables separately from requested clocks. Preflight VA/TX transitions and mux fallback, roll back only new acquisitions, never drain global CCF enabled state. Native FS sequence order and duplicate-register writes retained.",
  "error_limit": "Void native FS/all-clocks APIs log failures; internal helpers preserve errors. If a hardware rollback itself fails the error is logged; no hardware recovery claim.",
